1
00:00:00,025 --> 00:00:03,235
(Sheldon:)Of course, but not by myself.

2
00:00:03,403 --> 00:00:05,193
Really? Never?

3
00:00:05,363 --> 00:00:08,493
Well, once, when I was 15
and spending the summer...

4
00:00:08,658 --> 00:00:10,788
(Sheldon:)...at the Heidelberg Institute in Germany.

5
00:00:11,161 --> 00:00:14,581
- Studying abroad?
- No, visiting professor.

6
00:00:16,625 --> 00:00:20,795
(Sheldon:)Anyway, the local cuisine was a little more
sausage-based than I'm used to...

7
00:00:20,962 --> 00:00:23,092
(Sheldon:)...and the result
was an internal blitzkrieg...

8
00:00:23,256 --> 00:00:27,006
(Sheldon:)...with my lower intestine
playing the part of Czechoslovakia.

9
00:00:27,594 --> 00:00:29,764
And there was no one there
to take care of you?

10
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:33,390
No, my mom had to fly back to Texas
to help my dad...

11
00:00:33,558 --> 00:00:37,268
(Sheldon:)...because the house had slipped off
the cinder blocks again.

12
00:00:38,021 --> 00:00:40,561
(Leonard:)- Again?
- It was tornado season.

13
00:00:40,732 --> 00:00:42,982
And it was an aluminum house.

14
00:00:44,444 --> 00:00:48,114
(Sheldon:)Anyway, the housekeeper in the faculty
residence didn't speak any English.

15
00:00:48,281 --> 00:00:50,701
(Sheldon:)When I finally managed
to convince her I was sick...

16
00:00:50,867 --> 00:00:54,247
(Sheldon:)...she said,
"Möchtest du eine Darmspülung?"

17
00:00:54,621 --> 00:00:56,081
(Penny:)What does that mean?

18
00:00:56,248 --> 00:01:02,018
(Sheldon:)Based on what happened next, I assume
it means, "Would you like an enema?"

